Hello Eric,

There were two performance problems with vfast in V5.1B PK3 (BL24).

The first problem was a memory leak, which was fixed in V5.1B PK5
(BL25).

The second problem could cause vfast to consume too much cpu while it
is scanning a file's AdvFS extents.  This could be the problem you were
seeing, and it is fixed in V5.1B-3 (BL26).

So, the problem could be fixed by upgrading to V5.1B-3, or there exists
a CSP (patch) which contains both these fixes for installation on V5.1B
PK3.  The CSP Kit is T64KIT0024300-V51BB24-20041124.tar, and can be
obtained from the HP Support Center.

Hope this helps,
Charlie Franks



